pkg:Evidence_v1_25_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.25.0 (repeated version drift fixed)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: user's correct, direct finding -- 'You gave me the exact 1.4.0 file not a new one.' Same drift class as two turns ago, caught a second time: STORY-11's two real content changes were both committed to the same filename without a version bump. While fixing, read a directly relevant handover that landed in the Ontologies repo this session (VAF_HANDOVER_drift-retrospective_v1_0_0.md, another lineage's own real drift analysis) -- its diagnosis applies here word for word: technical verification (Playwright, pyshacl) ran with full rigor every time, but the procedural version-bump check did not run with the same automatic regularity. Bumped all 4 real stage files to v1_5_0, re-establishing Cross.D; confirmed both of STORY-11's real fixes survived the rename intact, not assumed. Updated the register's 3 live AcceptanceCriterion filename references. Re-verified: all Stage1-3 gates PASS fresh, real Playwright 0 errors, pipeline order unaffected, full SHACL 0 violations. Adopting a standing practice going forward: a mechanical Cross.D check (do all 4 stage files share one version token) after every edit that touches page/domain/research/document content, not only when explicitly asked."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "1c7f3bfb8924e5640a8e304dc19888172e05ec4663d2e1914a7d2590100ca62e"^^xsd:string .
